{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song of ascents.</b> Now in the psalm above he mentioned 'I will cause a horn to sprout for David,' and the meaning is the house of David. He mentioned that they would be one assembly in the days of Solomon with his brothers, and the word 'thing' is missing. And so it is: 'Behold, how good and how pleasant a thing' — for 'good' and 'pleasant' are adjectives and the modified noun is missing. The meaning also hints at the priests, or the correct understanding is that 'brothers' refers to the association of the priests. And the meaning of 'also' is upon the high priest."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 133, :notes {0 "The phrase 'the psalm above' refers to Psalm 132:17 ('there I will cause a horn to sprout for David'); 'אצמיח' preserves Ibn Ezra's spelling of the quoted phrase."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:40.907428233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}